From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode-port <port@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:53:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] D218 server: a session shell command that cannot start is a
 typed error

Upstream: POST /api/session/:id/shell records a "failed to start" notice in the session when the command
cannot start, then turns the failure into a defect, so the request answers 500 with an empty body (a NUL
character, or a command longer than the system can pass to the shell).
Fixed: Session.shell keeps the start failure typed, and the route answers it the way POST /api/shell does since D217
(the mapping moves to handlers/shell-error.ts and is shared): 400 InvalidRequestError (invalid_command, or
invalid_cwd when the session directory cannot be entered), otherwise 500 UnknownError with a log reference. The
session still gets its notice.
Scenarios: shell-api.test.ts "run commands in a session as the user" (two new requests and the inbox)
Upstream tests: packages/core/test/session-shell.test.ts asserts the start failure is typed; client and openapi.json
regenerated

